# Figma / Frame Component Conventions

## Image handling
- **Next image imports** can return `{ src, height, width }`. For CSS `url()` (e.g. `backgroundImage`, `maskImage`), always use a string. Use the project `imgSrc()` helper when the same file is used in both `src/App.tsx` and Figma-import files:

```tsx
function imgSrc(img: string | { src: string; height?: number; width?: number }): string {
  return typeof img === "string" ? img : img.src;
}
// Usage:
style={{ backgroundImage: `url('${imgSrc(imgImage4)}')` }}
```

- In **Figma-import modules** (e.g. `Frame2147229266.tsx`), imports may use `figma:asset/...`; in app code they use `@/assets/...`. Do not mix the two in the same file; keep asset paths consistent per file.

## Frame components
- Frame components are presentational: keep them as pure functions returning JSX; avoid business logic.
- Preserve `data-name` where it helps trace back to Figma (e.g. `data-name="Mask group"`).
- Use Tailwind for layout/sizing when it matches the design; use inline `style` for one-off values (e.g. gradients, transforms, mask URLs).

## Assets
- Shared images live under `src/assets/`. Reference them via `@/assets/...` in app and lib code.
